15
00:00:35,635 --> 00:00:37,559
Now for the hash table, you learned that in

16
00:00:37,559 --> 00:00:39,418
the end it's just an array that works with

17
00:00:39,482 --> 00:00:40,364
indexes, you could say,

18
00:00:40,909 --> 00:00:42,993
but that we have a hashing function that

19
00:00:42,993 --> 00:00:45,654
translates keys which we as a developer want

20
00:00:45,654 --> 00:00:46,311
to work with

21
00:00:46,920 --> 00:00:49,148
into indexes which then can be stored.

22
00:00:49,806 --> 00:00:51,906
So therefore, we'll now need to build the

23
00:00:51,906 --> 00:00:54,871
hashing function on our own and then build a

